SWEET WLAN stage 3 run C (patch 0131, W-D3 step 2, docs/research/43 rows W11..W13), behind boot-arg sweetwlan=5 (level 5 = run B of 0130, then W11-W13; levels 1-4 are byte-identical in behaviour to 0130).
W11 the NVRAM text: the "NVRM" entry of the 0128 container, CRC-checked before W0 (like the image), run through a pure C port of Broadcom's process_nvram_vars() (bcmutils.c:5101-5146) and of what its caller does (dhd_pcie.c:4208-4253: last
input byte forced to NUL, length rounded up to 4, one more NUL), stored at ram_end - 4 - varsize (varsize = ROUNDUP(len + 1, 4), dhd_pcie.c:10887-10891), zero padded, every word read back, then the whole text read back and its CRC32 compared.
W12 the length token (~w << 16) | (w & 0xFFFF), w = varsize / 4, at the last RAM word ram_end - 4 (dhd_pcie.c:10962-10970). W13 the rTLV 136 bytes below the text: 128 random bytes, the length word 0x80 (no checksum for the RNG type), the type word
0xFEEDC0DE (dhd_pcie.c:10480-10520, 17224-17236), read back; then the text and the token are read back once more and cfg 0x84 goes back to 0. The CA7 stays halted; nothing is released.
Pure part (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_wr.h): tuples SWT_WIN2_TAIL_C, SWT_NV_VARS, SWT_NV_TOKEN, SWT_NV_RTLV, SWT_WIN2_ZERO_C (run 3, flag SWT_TW for the three tail kinds), still the one swl_wr(): a tail tuple carries no value and no address, swl_wr() computes the next
word of the kind the address lies in (swl_tw_kind, swl_tw_word) and its address from ram_end and varsize (swl_geo_get) for every store; the table only bounds them at compile time. The whole tail must lie in the window 0x400000 (offset = backplane - 0x400000):
a RAM end that puts any of it lower is refused after W7, before the first image word (the geometry was not observed; deny by default). A consumed ONCE tuple or a tail tuple of another kind hands the store to the next matching tuple of an allowed
run (swl_wr_pick), so the second cfg 0x84 write and a zero text word at the last-word address need no second table of values. Entropy: swl_wbus.rng, injectable; the glue passes read_random() (bsd/sys/random.h, registered by patch 0014 at
STARTUP_RANK_FIRST of EARLY_BOOT); a failing or all-zero draw stops before W0.
Glue (bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c): sw_fw_note() keeps the NVRM entry too, a 27 KB scratch buffer, sw3_rng(), level 5 accepted. sw3_wr() is unchanged (BAR2 window 0x400000 and cfg 0x84 as 0 / 0x400000 were already allowed by 0130).
The final line of level 5: "SWEET WLAN: stage 3 level 5 done vars=<varsize> token=<hex> crc=<hex>", crc = CRC32 of the NVRAM region as read back.
Host tests shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c and shim/wlan_nv_host_test.c (the process_nvram_vars port: hand-derived known answers and a differently structured reference), mutants tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: not yet reviewed.

